{
  "case_id": "2024-24-304",
  "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument next in Case 24-304, Laboratory Corporation of America versus Davis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: The -- in this case, there have been a number of orders, and it seems as though the one that we have before us is the May order, which is inoperative. Would you spend a minute on why we still -- we have jurisdiction over the May order when there have been subsequent orders?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Francisco",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. FRANCISCO: And the mechanism has to be one that protects the defendant's rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, I -- I -- I'm having -- I'd like -- I want to follow up on on your answer to Justice Alito. When does a party become -- when does a party become a part of a litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Francisco",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. FRANCISCO: And that's where I fundamentally disagree with you, because that's only true if they win. If they lose, if the class is certified and they lose, the entire class is bound by that adverse judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Only --so you can never have an uninjured person in a class definition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: What happens to you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "And, as I said, if you were to do that -- and -- and I would strongly urge you not to -- I would be vigorously arguing for anything I could think of to allow us to appeal that August order well past the 14-day period of limitations under 28(f), and I would do my best to succeed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. I hear you saying at bottom that it violates Article III to include uninjured people in the class definition and that it violates Rule 23 if there are lots of uninjured people in the class definition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sopan Joshi",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "This Court has frequently said that Rule 23 requires all class members to share the same injury. We think that includes an Article III injury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: So what would you do at the early stages of the litigation, say, post-certification, and -- and you find injured -- uninjured parties in the -- in the class?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Why would that be the case, though? Because you have uninjured people in the party that you've now found."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So an Article III injury is required? It's a backdoor way of getting to Petitioner's position, I think."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Joshi)",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "If -- if you have a class in which Article III injury is not present for some but is -- is present for the others, that's just not going to meet the commonality standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus (Mr. Joshi)",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0004-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 107,
        "start": 107
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "As an amicus, we're poorly situated to take a strong view of matters, but, that said, I think -- I think Petitioners have the better of the argument, and what I would rely on are two things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 111,
        "start": 111
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: I guess I'm still\nstruggling with why isn't the sensible and\nreasonable manner of applying Rule 23 the way\nthat, as Justice Kagan says, we always do, that\nwe look at commonality or the district courts\nlook at commonality and predominance sort of in\nthe aggregate with all of the issues on the\ntable, there aren't directed to one or another\nto say that if this particular issue does not\nhave commonality, you can't certify the class.\nAnd that seems to be what you are saying."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 112,
        "start": 112
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Let me ask you a\nquestion. Do those cases talk about those\ninjuries in the context of the harm being an\nelement of the claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0005-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 116,
        "start": 116
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "brief in opposition did not raise this\njurisdictional problem. It did raise the -- the\nfundamental problem that in -- in the\nRespondents' view, the question presented is not\npresented by this case and other preservation\nissues."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0005-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 118,
        "start": 118
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, why would it\nbe --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Defendants",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0005-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 125,
        "start": 125
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "They said this is no\nrefinement at all. This proposed definition,\nthe August definition, is -- is broader than the\nexisting one and clearly includes those who have\nno injury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0005-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 131,
        "start": 131
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right? So,\nwhether it's under Article III or it's under\nRule 23, according to the SG, that you can't\nprove that. What's your point on that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 132,
        "start": 132
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Well, Mr. Gupta,\nthat -- that's the question that we didn't get\nto in Acheson, right? There are arguments that\nracial discrimination and other kinds of\ndiscrimination are different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gupta",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 132,
        "start": 132
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "our position has been\nall along that the -- the -- everyone in this\nclass is injured, and that's what the lower\ncourts, I think, recognized."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 141,
        "start": 141
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Do you think the\namicus briefs are wrong then? They're just not\nunderstanding their own interest? The\ninterest -- the amicus briefs on the other side."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 147,
        "start": 147
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, to return to a\nquestion that's a great favorite, do you think\nthis Ninth Circuit rule about material versus\nimmaterial changes is jurisdictional, or is it a\nclaims-processing rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0007-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 153,
        "start": 153
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Class-wide judgments and their finality and their preclusive effect under our current law is predicated on adequate representation and due process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0007-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 154,
        "start": 154
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Here's what plaintiffs argued to the district court when it urged the district court to adopt the August definition. It moved to to recline -- to refine the class definition, and it assured the court that it was \"identical in every way to the original May definition.\" And it assured it that it had not changed the \"substance\" of the class."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0007-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 156,
        "start": 156
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "acknowledged that when it comes to a class loss, the only consequence is that you're going to end up binding a class even if it includes members over whom the Court lacked jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 0.0,
